( lib/mouse.ux — button-edge polls over game-read mouse state.
  Position and scroll stay raw port reads (there is nothing to
  abstract: `Mouse.x` / `Mouse.y`); this module is the input/state
  half, mirroring menu_poll. Games declare Mouse (copy this block,
  grounded in uxn2/src/uxn2.c mouse_* — note scroll lives at 9a/9c
  as one-shot deltas with inverted Y, zeroed after the vector):
      device Mouse 144 {
          vector: 2
          x: 2
          y: 2
          state: 1
          pad: 3
          scrollx: 2
          scrolly: 2
      }
  Button masks follow the emulator's SDL mapping
  (get_mouse_button: left 1, middle 4, right 3 — right overlaps
  bit 0, so test it with ==, the rest with &). Wire
  `Mouse.vector = &on_mouse` and poll `Mouse.state` there (or once
  per frame); headless runs can't click, so the gate below feeds
  synthetic states. )

MOUSE_LEFT :: 1;
MOUSE_MIDDLE :: 4;
MOUSE_RIGHT :: 3;
MOUSE_X1 :: 2;

mouse_last: u8 = 0;

( Bits newly down since the last poll (edge, not hold). Call with
  Mouse.state whenever the mouse vector fires (or per frame). )
mouse_poll :: fn(cur: u8) -> u8 {
    pressed: u8 = cur & (mouse_last ^ 255);
    mouse_last = cur;
    return pressed;
}
